     orders of d_tau^m w on the slice, m = 2..6: [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]
  P4a d_tau^m w has order exactly N + 1 - m (one lam^-1 per derivative): polynomial: pass 
  P4b control: the claim 'order N - 1 at every m' fails (m = 3): pass 
P5  Lemma 11.0 as written: the exponent recursion
  P5a the record's split: floor((N + 2)/2) <= max(4, N - 3) for N = 1..199: pass 
     P(N), N = 7..16: [7, 11, 12, 16, 17, 18, 22, 23, 27, 28]
     P(N)/N at N = 40, 80, 120, 160: [2.05, 2.2, 2.225, 2.237]
  P5b finite at every order N <= 160 (polynomial in lam^-1 at each order, K-independent): pass 
  P5c the written bookkeeping gives P(N) <= 9N/4 for 7 <= N <= 160 (P(40) = 82, P(160) = 358); control: P(N) <= N fails (N = 8): pass P(8) = 11, P(40) = 82, P(160) = 358
  P5d control: the reverse split asks for a pointwise order not yet controlled: pass ('uncontrolled', 7, 7)
P6  the sharp reading u_1 = a + w (Proposition 9.8 at order k): natural exponents
  P6a the recursion closes at P(N) = N for N <= 40 (Q(n) = n - 1 from a and w): pass 
  P6b the scaled bootstrap closes at K'_0 = 17 (2K' - 5 > K'); control: at K' = 5 it does not: pass 
P7  Lemma 11.2 and Proposition 11.1: the coefficients and the remainders
